<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sri_Lanka_national_cricket_team> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Test [kit](:Cricket_clothing_and_equipment)****ODI kit****T20I kit**The **Sri Lanka men's national cricket team**, (Template:Lang-si, Template:Lang-ta nicknamed **The Lions**, represents [Sri Lanka](:Sri_Lanka) in men's international [cricket](:Cricket). It is a Full Member of the [International Cricket Council](:International_Cricket_Council) (ICC) with [Test](:Test_cricket), [One-Day International](:One-Day_International) (ODI) and [T20 International](:T20_International) (T20I) status. The team first played international cricket (as Ceylon) in 1926–27, and were later awarded [Test](:Test_cricket) status in 1981, which made Sri Lanka the eighth Test cricket playing nation. The team is administered by [Sri Lanka Cricket](:Sri_Lanka_Cricket).Sri Lanka's national cricket team achieved considerable success beginning in the 1990s, rising from [underdog](:Underdog_%28competition%29) status to winning the [Cricket World Cup](:Cricket_World_Cup) in [1996](:1996_Cricket_World_Cup), under the captaincy of [Arjuna Ranatunga](:Arjuna_Ranatunga). Since then, the team has continued to be a force in international cricket. The Sri Lankan cricket team reached the finals of the [2007](:2007_Cricket_World_Cup) and [2011](:2011_Cricket_World_Cup) [Cricket World Cups](:Cricket_World_Cup) consecutively. They ended up being runners-up on both occasions.Sri Lanka won the [Cricket World Cup](:Cricket_World_Cup) in [1996](:1996_Cricket_World_Cup) (vs Australia), the [ICC Champions Trophy](:ICC_Champions_Trophy) in [2002](:2002_ICC_Champions_Trophy) (co-champions with [India](:India_national_cricket_team%29), and the [ICC T20 World Cup](:ICC_T20_World_Cup) in 2014 (vs India). They have been consecutive runners up in the [2007](:2007_Cricket_World_Cup) and [2011 Cricket World Cups](:2011_Cricket_World_Cup), and have been runners up in the ICC T20 World Cup in [2009](:2009_ICC_World_Twenty20) and [2012](:2012_ICC_World_Twenty20). The Sri Lankan cricket team currently holds several world records, including the world record for the highest team total in [Test cricket](:Test_cricket)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
