<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Helsinki> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Helsinki** ( [*HEL-sink-ee*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key) or   [*hel-SINK-ee*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key); Template:IPA-fi; Template:Lang-sv, Template:IPA-sv is the [capital](:Capital_city), [primate](:Primate_city), and [most populous city](:List_of_cities_and_towns_in_Finland) of [Finland](:Finland). Located on the shore of the [Gulf of Finland](:Gulf_of_Finland), it is the seat of the region of [Uusimaa](:Uusimaa) in southern Finland, and has a population of 684,589. The [city's urban area](:Helsinki_urban_area) has a population of 1,268,296, making it by far the [most populous urban area in Finland](:List_of_urban_areas_in_Finland_by_population) as well as the country's most important center for politics, education, finance, culture, and research; while [Tampere](:Tampere) in the [Pirkanmaa](:Pirkanmaa) region, located 179 kilometres (111 mi) to the north from Helsinki, is the second largest urban area in Finland. Helsinki is located 80 kilometres (50 mi) north of [Tallinn, Estonia](:Tallinn%2C_Estonia), 400 km (250 mi) east of [Stockholm, Sweden](:Stockholm%2C_Sweden), and 300 km (190 mi) west of [Saint Petersburg, Russia](:Saint_Petersburg%2C_Russia). It has [close historical ties](:History_of_Helsinki) with these three cities.Together with the cities of [Espoo](:Espoo), [Vantaa](:Vantaa), and [Kauniainen](:Kauniainen) (and surrounding commuter towns, including the eastern neighboring municipality of [Sipoo](:Sipoo%29), Helsinki forms the [Greater Helsinki](:Greater_Helsinki) metropolitan area, which has a population of over 1.5 million. Often considered to be Finland's only metropolis, it is the world's [northernmost metro area](:List_of_northernmost_items%23Cities_and_settlements) with over one million people as well as the northernmost capital of an [EU member state](:Member_state_of_the_European_Union). After [Copenhagen](:Copenhagen) and Stockholm, Helsinki is the [third largest municipality in the Nordic countries](:List_of_the_most_populated_municipalities_in_the_Nordic_countries). [Finnish](:Finnish_language) and [Swedish](:Swedish_language) are both official languages. The city is served by the international [Helsinki Airport](:Helsinki_Airport), located in the neighboring city of Vantaa, with frequent service to many destinations in Europe and Asia.Helsinki was the [World Design Capital](:World_Design_Capital) for 2012, the venue for the [1952 Summer Olympics](:1952_Summer_Olympics), and the host of the [52nd Eurovision Song Contest in 2007](:Eurovision_Song_Contest_2007).Helsinki has one of the world's highest standards of urban living. In 2011, the British magazine *[Monocle](:Monocle_%28UK_magazine%29)* ranked Helsinki the world's most liveable city in its [liveable cities index](:Most_livable_cities%23Monocle%27s_Quality_of_Life_Survey). In the [Economist Intelligence Unit's](:Economist_Intelligence_Unit) 2016 liveability survey, Helsinki was ranked ninth among 140 cities. In July 2021, the American magazine *[Time](:Time_%28magazine%29)* ranked Helsinki one of the greatest places in the world in 2021 as a city that \"can grow into a sprouting cultural nest in the future,\" and which has already been known in the world as an [environmental](:Environmental) pioneer. An international *Cities of Choice* survey conducted in 2021 by the consulting firm [Boston Consulting Group](:Boston_Consulting_Group) and the BCG Henderson Institute raised Helsinki the third best city in the world to live, with [London](:London) and [New York City](:New_York_City) ranking the first and the second. Also, together with [Rovaniemi](:Rovaniemi) in the [Lapland](:Lapland_%28Finland%29) region, Helsinki is one of Finland's most significant tourist cities in terms of [foreign tourism](:Tourism)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
