<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chicago_Bears> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**[National Football League](:National_Football_League) ([1920](:1920_NFL_season)–present)****[1970](:1970_Chicago_Bears_season) due to renovations to [Wrigley Field](:Wrigley_Field):****[2002](:2002_Chicago_Bears_season) due to renovations to [Soldier Field](:Soldier_Field):**The **Chicago Bears** are a professional [American football](:American_football) team based in [Chicago](:Chicago). The Bears compete in the [National Football League](:National_Football_League) (NFL) as a member club of the league's [National Football Conference](:National_Football_Conference) (NFC) [North](:NFC_North) division. The Bears have won nine [NFL Championships](:History_of_the_National_Football_League_championship), including one [Super Bowl](:Super_Bowl_XX), and hold the NFL record for the most enshrinees in the [Pro Football Hall of Fame](:Pro_Football_Hall_of_Fame) and the most [retired jersey](:Retired_jersey) numbers. The Bears have also recorded more victories than any other NFL franchise, except for the [Green Bay Packers](:Green_Bay_Packers), who they are tied with.The franchise was founded in [Decatur, Illinois](:Decatur%2C_Illinois), on September 20, 1919 and became professional on September 17, 1920, and moved to Chicago in 1921. It is one of only two remaining franchises from the NFL's founding in 1920, along with the [Arizona Cardinals](:Arizona_Cardinals), which was originally also in Chicago. The team played home games at [Wrigley Field](:Wrigley_Field) on Chicago's [North Side](:North_Side%2C_Chicago) through the 1970 season; they now play at [Soldier Field](:Soldier_Field) on the [Near South Side](:Near_South_Side%2C_Chicago), adjacent to [Lake Michigan](:Lake_Michigan). The Bears have a [long-standing rivalry](:Bears%E2%80%93Packers_rivalry) with the Green Bay Packers.The team headquarters, [Halas Hall](:Halas_Hall), is in the Chicago suburb of [Lake Forest, Illinois](:Lake_Forest%2C_Illinois). The Bears practice at adjoining facilities there during the season, and began hosting Training Camp at Halas Hall in 2020 after major renovations."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
