<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sandy_Herd_(footballer)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Andrew Clark \"Sandy\" Herd (4 October 1903 – 1 December 1984) was a Scottish professional footballer. A miner by trade, Herd started his senior career with Dundee, whom he joined from junior side Hearts of Beath, in 1923. He joined Dunfermline Athletic a year later, helping them to win the Division Two title in 1925–26. He was signed by Hearts in 1927 in a £250 transfer deal, with moving to Dunfermline as part of the agreement."@en .
