<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Minnetonka,_Minnesota> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Minnetonka** ( [*MIN-i-TONG-kə*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is a city in [Hennepin County](:Hennepin_County%2C_Minnesota), [Minnesota](:Minnesota), United States. A western suburb of the [Twin Cities](:Twin_Cities), Minnetonka is located about 10 miles (16 km) west of downtown [Minneapolis](:Minneapolis). As of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census), the city's population was 53,781.Minnetonka is the home of [Cargill](:Cargill), the country's [largest](:List_of_largest_private_non-governmental_companies_by_revenue) privately owned company, and [UnitedHealth Group](:UnitedHealth_Group), the state's largest publicly owned company. [Interstate 494](:Interstate_494) runs through the city while [Interstate 394](:Interstate_394) ([U.S. Route 12](:U%2ES%2E_Route_12%29) and [U.S. Route 169](:U%2ES%2E_Route_169) are situated along the suburb's northern and eastern boundaries respectively."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
