<http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Bacon_(footballer)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "John Bacon (born 23 March 1973 in Dublin) is an Irish former footballer. Bacon joined Arsenal in July 1989 and spent four years as a member of the youth side, winning a South East Counties League title in 1990-91. He was also capped four times by the Irish Under 21 team. He never made a first-team appearance, and was loaned to Shamrock Rovers in January 1992. He made his League of Ireland Premier Division debut for Rovers against Dundalk on 26 January 1992 and in total scored three times in ten league appearances that season."@en .
