<http://dbpedia.org/resource/AIK_IF> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Allmänna Idrottsklubben Ishockeyförening** (abbreviated *AIK IF*, also known as *AIK Hockey*, often abbreviated *AIK* in hockey subjects), is the [ice hockey](:Ice_hockey) department of sports club [Allmänna Idrottsklubben](:Allm%C3%A4nna_Idrottsklubben) based in [Stockholm](:Stockholm), [Sweden](:Sweden). Since 2014, AIK's men's team compete in [HockeyAllsvenskan](:HockeyAllsvenskan), the second tier of [ice hockey in Sweden](:Ice_hockey_in_Sweden), following a four-year spell in the top flight, the [SHL](:Swedish_Hockey_League). The women's team competes in [Riksserien](:Riksserien), the highest division of women's ice hockey. AIK's home games are mainly played at [Hovet](:Hovet), which seats 8,050 spectators, though some high-profile games may be played at [Avicii Arena](:Avicii_Arena) which has a larger capacity of 13,850.In the team's 103-year history, AIK has played 66 seasons in Sweden's top division, 27 of which in the SHL. They have won the [Le Mat Trophy](:Le_Mat_Trophy) as [Swedish champions in ice hockey](:List_of_Swedish_ice_hockey_champions) seven times (in 1934, 1935, 1938, 1946, 1947, 1982, and 1984) and have been runners-up an additional six times (in 1930, 1936, 1940, 1968, 1978, and 1981)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
