<http://dbpedia.org/resource/José_Zalazar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "José Luis Zalazar Rodríguez (born 26 October 1963) is a Uruguayan retired footballer who played mostly as an attacking midfielder. Nicknamed El Oso (Bear), he played most of his career in Spain, especially with Albacete Balompié, being part of the club's most long tenure in La Liga. He was also notable for his strong and accurate right-foot shot, as demonstrated with several goals from long distance, particularly from free kicks. An Uruguay international for nearly one decade, Zalazar represented the country at the 1986 World Cup."@en .
