<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Miami_Dolphins> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**[National Football League](:National_Football_League) ([1970](:1970_NFL_season)–present)**The **Miami Dolphins** are a professional [American football](:American_football) team based in the [Miami metropolitan area](:Miami_metropolitan_area). They compete in the [National Football League](:National_Football_League) (NFL) as a member team of the league's [American Football Conference](:American_Football_Conference) (AFC) [East](:AFC_East) division. The team plays its home games at [Hard Rock Stadium](:Hard_Rock_Stadium), located in the northern suburb of [Miami Gardens, Florida](:Miami_Gardens%2C_Florida). The team is currently owned by [Stephen M. Ross](:Stephen_M%2E_Ross). The Dolphins are the oldest professional sports team in Florida. Of the four AFC East teams, the Dolphins are the only team in the division that was not a charter member of the [American Football League](:American_Football_League) (AFL). The Dolphins were also one of the first professional football teams in the southeast, along with the [Atlanta Falcons](:Atlanta_Falcons).The Dolphins were founded by attorney-politician [Joe Robbie](:Joe_Robbie) and actor-comedian [Danny Thomas](:Danny_Thomas). They began play in the AFL in [1966](:1966_Miami_Dolphins_season). The region had not had a professional football team since the days of the [Miami Seahawks](:Miami_Seahawks), who played in the [All-America Football Conference](:All-America_Football_Conference) in 1946, before becoming the first incarnation of the [Baltimore Colts](:Baltimore_Colts_%281947%E2%80%9350%29). For the first few years, the Dolphins' full-time training camp and practice facilities were at [Saint Andrew's School](:Saint_Andrew%27s_School_%28Boca_Raton%2C_Florida%29), a private, boys boarding prep school in Boca Raton. Miami joined the NFL as a result of the 1970 [AFL–NFL merger](:AFL%E2%80%93NFL_merger).The team played in its first [Super Bowl](:Super_Bowl) in [Super Bowl VI](:Super_Bowl_VI), losing to the [Dallas Cowboys](:Dallas_Cowboys), 24–3. [The following year](:1972_Miami_Dolphins_season), the Dolphins completed the NFL's only [perfect season](:Perfect_season), culminating in a Super Bowl win, winning all 14 of their regular-season games, and all three of their playoff games, including [Super Bowl VII](:Super_Bowl_VII). They were the third NFL team to accomplish a perfect [regular season](:National_Football_League_regular_season), and the first team to do so after the AFL-NFL merger, the time known as the Super Bowl era. The next year, the Dolphins won [Super Bowl VIII](:Super_Bowl_VIII), becoming the first team to appear in three consecutive Super Bowls, and the second team (the first AFL/AFC team) to win back-to-back championships. Miami also appeared in [Super Bowl XVII](:Super_Bowl_XVII) and [Super Bowl XIX](:Super_Bowl_XIX), losing both games.For most of their early history, the Dolphins were coached by [Don Shula](:Don_Shula), the most successful head coach in professional football history in terms of total games won. Under Shula, the Dolphins posted losing records in only two of his 26 seasons as the head coach. During the period spanning 1983 to the end of 1999, quarterback [Dan Marino](:Dan_Marino) became one of the most prolific passers in NFL history, breaking numerous league passing records. Marino led the Dolphins to five division titles, 10 playoff appearances, and an appearance in Super Bowl XIX before retiring following the [1999 season](:1999_Miami_Dolphins_season).Since Marino's retirement, they have experienced mediocre levels of success and have just four playoff appearances ([2000](:2000%E2%80%9301_NFL_playoffs), [2001](:2001%E2%80%9302_NFL_playoffs), [2008](:2008%E2%80%9309_NFL_playoffs), and [2016](:2016%E2%80%9317_NFL_playoffs%29) and two division titles ([2000](:2000_Miami_Dolphins_season) and [2008](:2008_Miami_Dolphins_season%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HPK> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Hämeenlinnan Pallokerho (HPK) is a professional ice hockey team in the Liiga, the top men's ice hockey league in Finland. Their home ice is the Ritari-areena in Hämeenlinna. HPK was established in 1929. The parent club of the team is HPK Edustusjääkiekko ry and the team is sometimes promoted as the \"Hockey Playing Knights,\" with a logo representing a knight's helmet. HPK won their first SM-liiga championship in 2006 and the second in 2019."@en .
