<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Toronto> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Toronto** (  [*tə-RON-toh*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key); locally  or ) is the [capital city](:Capital_city) of the [Canadian province](:Provinces_and_territories_of_Canada) of [Ontario](:Ontario). With a recorded population of 2,794,356 in 2021, it is the [most populous city in Canada](:List_of_the_largest_municipalities_in_Canada_by_population) and the [fourth most populous city in North America](:List_of_North_American_cities_by_population). The city is the anchor of the [Golden Horseshoe](:Golden_Horseshoe), an urban agglomeration of 9,765,188 people (as of 2021) surrounding the western end of [Lake Ontario](:Lake_Ontario), while the [Greater Toronto Area](:Greater_Toronto_Area) proper had a 2021 population of 6,712,341. Toronto is an international centre of business, finance, arts, sports and culture, and is recognized as one of the most [multicultural](:Multiculturalism) and [cosmopolitan](:Cosmopolitanism) cities in the world.[Indigenous peoples](:Indigenous_peoples_in_Canada) have travelled through and inhabited the Toronto area, located on a broad sloping [plateau](:Plateau) interspersed with [rivers, deep ravines, and urban forest](:Toronto_ravine_system), for more than 10,000 years. After the broadly disputed [Toronto Purchase](:Toronto_Purchase), when the [Mississauga](:Mississaugas) surrendered the area to the [British Crown](:The_Crown), the British established the town of [York](:York%2C_Upper_Canada) in 1793 and later designated it as the capital of [Upper Canada](:Upper_Canada). During the [War of 1812](:War_of_1812), the town was the site of the [Battle of York](:Battle_of_York) and suffered heavy damage by [American troops](:United_States_Armed_Forces). York was [renamed](:Name_of_Toronto) and incorporated in 1834 as the [city of Toronto](:Old_Toronto). It was designated as the capital of the province of Ontario in 1867 during [Canadian Confederation](:Canadian_Confederation). The [city proper](:City_proper) has since expanded past its original limits through both [annexation](:Merger_%28politics%29) and [amalgamation](:Amalgamation_of_Toronto) to its current area of 630.2 km2 (243.3 sq mi).The diverse population of Toronto reflects its current and historical role as an important destination for [immigrants to Canada](:Immigration_to_Canada). More than half of residents were born outside of Canada, more than half of residents belong to a [visible minority](:Visible_minority) group, and over 200 distinct [ethnic origins](:Ethnic_group) are represented among its inhabitants. While the majority of Torontonians speak [English](:English_language) as their primary language, over 160 languages are spoken in the city. The mayor of Toronto is elected by direct popular vote to serve as the [chief executive](:Head_of_government) of the city. The [Toronto City Council](:Toronto_City_Council) is a [unicameral](:Unicameralism) legislative body, comprising 25 councillors since the [2018 municipal election](:2018_Toronto_municipal_election), representing geographical [wards](:Ward_%28electoral_subdivision%29) throughout the city.Toronto is a prominent centre for music, theatre, motion picture production, and television production, and is home to the headquarters of Canada's major national [broadcast networks](:Broadcast_network) and [media](:Media_in_Toronto) outlets. Its varied [cultural institutions](:Culture_in_Toronto), which include numerous [museums and galleries](:List_of_museums_in_Toronto), [festivals and public events](:Annual_events_in_Toronto), entertainment districts, [national historic sites](:List_of_National_Historic_Sites_of_Canada_in_Toronto), and [sports activities](:Sports_in_Toronto), attract over 43 million [tourists](:Tourism_in_Toronto) each year. Toronto is known for its many [skyscrapers and high-rise buildings](:List_of_tallest_buildings_in_Toronto), in particular the [tallest free-standing structure](:List_of_tallest_freestanding_structures) on land outside of [Asia](:Asia), the [CN Tower](:CN_Tower).The city is home to the [Toronto Stock Exchange](:Toronto_Stock_Exchange), the headquarters of Canada's [five largest banks](:Big_Five_%28banks%29), and the headquarters of many large Canadian and multinational corporations. Its [economy](:Economy_of_Toronto) is highly diversified with strengths in technology, design, financial services, life sciences, education, arts, fashion, aerospace, environmental innovation, food services, and tourism. Toronto is the third-largest [tech hub](:List_of_technology_centers) in North America after [Silicon Valley](:Silicon_Valley) and [New York City](:New_York_City), and the fastest growing."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
