<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Casper,_Wyoming> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Casper** is a city in, and the [county seat](:County_seat) of, [Natrona County](:Natrona_County%2C_Wyoming), [Wyoming](:Wyoming), United States. Casper is the second-largest city in the state, with the population at 59,038 as of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census). Only [Cheyenne](:Cheyenne%2C_Wyoming), the state capital, is larger. Casper is nicknamed \"The Oil City\" and has a long history of oil boomtown and cowboy culture, dating back to the development of the nearby [Salt Creek Oil Field](:Salt_Creek_Oil_Field).Casper is located in east central Wyoming."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
