<http://dbpedia.org/resource/University_of_Georgia> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\"To serve\" was later added to the motto without changing the seal; the Latin motto directly translates as \"To teach and to inquire into the nature of things.\"The **University of Georgia** (**UGA** or **Georgia**) is a [public](:Public_university) [land-grant](:Land-grant_university) [research university](:Research_university) with its main campus in [Athens, Georgia](:Athens%2C_Georgia). Founded in 1785, it is one of the [oldest public universities in the United States](:Oldest_public_university_in_the_United_States). The [flagship](:Flagship_university) school of the [University System of Georgia](:University_System_of_Georgia), it has been ranked by major [institutional rankings](:College_and_university_rankings_in_the_United_States) among the best public universities in the United States.The university is [classified](:Carnegie_Classification_of_Institutions_of_Higher_Education) among \"R1: Doctoral Universities – Very high research activity,\" and as having \"more selective\" undergraduate admissions, the most selective admissions category, while the [ACT Assessment Student Report](:ACT_%28test%29) places UGA admissions in the \"Highly Selective\" category, the highest classification. Among public universities, the University of Georgia is one of the nation's top three producers of [Rhodes Scholars](:Rhodes_Scholarship) over the past two decades.In addition to the main campuses in Athens with their approximately 470 buildings, the university has two smaller campuses located in [Tifton](:Tifton%2C_Georgia) and [Griffin](:Griffin%2C_Georgia). The university has two [satellite campuses](:Satellite_campus) located in [Atlanta](:Atlanta%2C_Georgia) and [Lawrenceville](:Lawrenceville%2C_Georgia). The total acreage of the university in 30 [Georgia counties](:List_of_counties_in_Georgia_%28U%2ES%2E_state%29) is 41,539 acres (168.10 km2).The University of Georgia's intercollegiate sports teams, commonly known by their [Georgia Bulldogs](:Georgia_Bulldogs) name compete in [National Collegiate Athletic Association](:National_Collegiate_Athletic_Association) (NCAA) [Division I](:NCAA_Division_I) and the [Southeastern Conference](:Southeastern_Conference) (SEC).Notable alumni and attendees include current and former members of the [United States Senate](:United_States_Senate), members of the [United States House of Representatives](:United_States_House_of_Representatives), [federal judges](:Federal_judge), [Rhodes Scholars](:Rhodes_Scholarship), [Marshall Scholars](:Marshall_Scholarship), [MacArthur Fellows](:MacArthur_Fellows_Program) (the [\"Genius Grant\"](:MacArthur_Fellows_Program%29) winners, as well as [Pulitzer Prize](:Pulitzer_Prize) winners, a [United States Poet Laureate](:United_States_Poet_Laureate), [Emmy Award](:Emmy_Award) winners, [Grammy Award](:Grammy_Award) winners, and multiple [Super Bowl champions](:Super_Bowl_champions)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
