<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Franklin_Langham> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Franklin Langham** (born May 8, 1968) is an American [professional golfer](:Professional_golfer).Langham was born in [Thomson, Georgia](:Thomson%2C_Georgia). He played golf at the [University of Georgia](:University_of_Georgia) from 1989 to 1991 and was named an [All-American](:All-America) in 1991. He played on the [1991 Walker Cup](:1991_Walker_Cup) team.Langham played on the [PGA Tour](:PGA_Tour) in 1996, 1998-2002 and 2005 and on the [Nationwide Tour](:Nationwide_Tour) in 1993-95, 1997, 2003–04 and 2006–08. He has three victories on the Nationwide Tour and has had finished runner-up on four occasions in PGA Tour events. He best finish on the PGA Tour money list was 26th in 2000. His best finish at a [major](:Men%27s_major_golf_championship) was 7th place at the [2000 PGA Championship](:2000_PGA_Championship).The 2008 season saw Langham's final year on the Nationwide Tour."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
