<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vancouver_Canucks> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Vancouver Canucks** are a professional [ice hockey](:Ice_hockey) team based in [Vancouver](:Vancouver). They compete in the [National Hockey League](:National_Hockey_League) (NHL) as a member of the [Pacific Division](:Pacific_Division_%28NHL%29) of the [Western Conference](:Western_Conference_%28NHL%29), and play their home games at [Rogers Arena](:Rogers_Arena). [Bruce Boudreau](:Bruce_Boudreau) is the head coach, [Jim Rutherford](:Jim_Rutherford) serves as the president of hockey operations, and [Patrik Allvin](:Patrik_Allvin) serves as the general manager.The Canucks joined the league in [1970](:1970%E2%80%9371_NHL_season) as an [expansion team](:Expansion_team) along with the [Buffalo Sabres](:Buffalo_Sabres). In its NHL history, the team has advanced to the [Stanley Cup Finals](:Stanley_Cup_Finals) three times, losing to the [New York Islanders](:New_York_Islanders) in [1982](:1982_Stanley_Cup_Finals), the [New York Rangers](:New_York_Rangers) in [1994](:1994_Stanley_Cup_Finals) and the [Boston Bruins](:Boston_Bruins) in [2011](:2011_Stanley_Cup_Finals). They have won the [Presidents' Trophy](:Presidents%27_Trophy) in back-to-back seasons as the team with the league's best regular-season record in the [2010–11](:2010%E2%80%9311_NHL_season) and [2011–12](:2011%E2%80%9312_NHL_season) seasons. They won three division titles as a member of the [Smythe Division](:Smythe_Division) from 1974 to 1993, and seven titles as a member of the [Northwest Division](:Northwest_Division_%28NHL%29) from 1998 to 2013. The Canucks, along with the Sabres, are the two oldest teams to have never won the [Stanley Cup](:Stanley_Cup).The Canucks have retired six players' jerseys in their history—[Pavel Bure](:Pavel_Bure) (10), [Stan Smyl](:Stan_Smyl) (12), [Trevor Linden](:Trevor_Linden) (16), [Markus Naslund](:Markus_N%C3%A4slund) (19), [Daniel Sedin](:Daniel_Sedin) (22) and [Henrik Sedin](:Henrik_Sedin) (33); all but Bure and Daniel Sedin have served as team captain. All but Naslund were on one of the three Stanley Cup Finals rosters. Smyl has the distinction of being the only Canuck to have his jersey number retired at their former arena, [Pacific Coliseum](:Pacific_Coliseum)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
