<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leiden> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Leiden** (Template:IPA-nl; in [English](:English_language) and [archaic](:Archaism) [Dutch](:Dutch_language) also **Leyden**) is a [city](:List_of_cities_in_the_Netherlands_by_province) and [municipality](:List_of_municipalities_of_the_Netherlands) in the [province](:Provinces_of_the_Netherlands) of [South Holland](:South_Holland), [Netherlands](:Netherlands). The municipality of Leiden has a population of 119,713, but the city forms one densely connected agglomeration with its suburbs [Oegstgeest](:Oegstgeest), [Leiderdorp](:Leiderdorp), [Voorschoten](:Voorschoten) and [Zoeterwoude](:Zoeterwoude) with 206,647 inhabitants. The [Netherlands Central Bureau of Statistics](:Statistics_Netherlands) (CBS) further includes [Katwijk](:Katwijk) in the agglomeration which makes the total population of the Leiden urban agglomeration 270,879, and in the larger Leiden urban area also [Teylingen](:Teylingen), [Noordwijk](:Noordwijk), and [Noordwijkerhout](:Noordwijkerhout) are included with in total 348,868 inhabitants. Leiden is located on the [Oude Rijn](:Oude_Rijn_%28Utrecht_and_South_Holland%29), at a distance of some 20 km (12 mi) from [The Hague](:The_Hague) to its south and some 40 km (25 mi) from [Amsterdam](:Amsterdam) to its north. The recreational area of the Kaag Lakes ([Kagerplassen](:Kagerplassen%29) lies just to the northeast of Leiden.A [university city](:University_town) since 1575, Leiden has been one of [Europe](:Europe)'s most prominent scientific centres for more than four centuries. Leiden is a typical [university city](:University_town), university buildings are scattered throughout the city and the many students from all over the world give the city a bustling, vivid and international atmosphere. Many important scientific discoveries have been made here, giving rise to Leiden's motto: ‘City of Discoveries’. The city houses [Leiden University](:Leiden_University), the oldest university of the Netherlands, and [Leiden University Medical Center](:Leiden_University_Medical_Center). Leiden University is one of Europe's top universities, with thirteen Nobel Prize winners. It is a member of the League of European Research Universities and positioned highly in all international academic rankings. It is twinned with [Oxford](:Oxford), the location of the United Kingdom's oldest [university](:University_of_Oxford). Leiden University and Leiden University of Applied Sciences (Leidse Hogeschool) together have around 35,000 students. Modern scientific medical research and teaching started in the early 18th century in Leiden with Boerhaave.Leiden is a city with a rich cultural heritage, not only in science, but also in the arts. One of the world's most famous painters, [Rembrandt](:Rembrandt), was born and educated in Leiden. Other famous Leiden painters include [Lucas van Leyden](:Lucas_van_Leyden), [Jan van Goyen](:Jan_van_Goyen) and [Jan Steen](:Jan_Steen)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
