<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Miami_Marlins> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Miami Marlins** are an American [professional baseball](:Professional_baseball) team based in [Miami](:Miami). The Marlins compete in [Major League Baseball](:Major_League_Baseball) (MLB) as a member club of the [National League](:National_League) (NL) [East](:National_League_East) division. The club's home ballpark is [LoanDepot Park](:LoanDepot_Park).The franchise began play as an [expansion team in the 1993 season](:1993_Major_League_Baseball_expansion) as the **Florida Marlins**. The Marlins originally played home games at [Joe Robbie Stadium](:Hard_Rock_Stadium), which they shared with the [National Football League](:National_Football_League) (NFL)'s [Miami Dolphins](:Miami_Dolphins). In 2012, the team moved to LoanDepot Park (then known as Marlins Park), their first exclusive home and the first to be designed as a baseball park. As part of an agreement with park owner [Miami-Dade County](:Miami-Dade_County%2C_Florida) to use the stadium, the franchise also changed their name to the Miami Marlins prior to the 2012 season.The Marlins have qualified for the [postseason](:Major_League_Baseball_postseason) only three times, but won the [World Series](:World_Series) during their first two runs in [1997](:1997_World_Series) and [2003](:2003_World_Series). All three of their playoff appearances came as [wild card](:Wild_card_%28sports%29) teams, making them one of two MLB franchises (along with the [Colorado Rockies](:Colorado_Rockies%29) to have never won a division title, as well as the only franchise to have never appeared in back-to-back postseasons. The Marlins were also the first team to win the World Series as a wild card."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
