<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Minnesota_Vikings> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Minnesota Vikings** are a professional [American football](:American_football) team based in [Minneapolis](:Minneapolis). They compete in the [National Football League](:National_Football_League) (NFL) as a member club of the [National Football Conference](:National_Football_Conference) (NFC) [North](:NFC_North) division. Founded in 1960 as an [expansion team](:Expansion_team), the team began play the [following year](:1961_Minnesota_Vikings_season). They are named after the [Vikings](:Vikings) of medieval [Scandinavia](:Scandinavia), reflecting the prominent [Scandinavian American](:Scandinavian_American) culture of [Minnesota](:Minnesota). The team plays its home games at [U.S. Bank Stadium](:U%2ES%2E_Bank_Stadium) in the [Downtown East](:Downtown_East%2C_Minneapolis) section of Minneapolis.The Vikings have an all-time overall record of 524–451–11, the highest regular season and combined winning percentage among NFL franchises who have not won a [Super Bowl](:Super_Bowl), in addition the most playoff runs, division titles, and (tied with the [Buffalo Bills](:Buffalo_Bills%29) Super Bowl appearances. They also have the most conference championship appearances of non-winning Super Bowl teams, with them being one of three (along with the [Pittsburgh Steelers](:Pittsburgh_Steelers) and [Los Angeles Rams](:Los_Angeles_Rams%29) to appear in a conference championship every decade since the 1970s."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
