<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Al_Pedrique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Alfredo José Pedrique García** (Template:IPA-es, born August 11, 1960) is a [Venezuelan](:Venezuelans) [professional baseball](:Professional_baseball) player, [coach](:Coach_%28baseball%29), and [manager](:Manager_%28baseball%29). He played in [Major League Baseball](:Major_League_Baseball) (MLB) as a [shortstop](:Shortstop) for the [New York Mets](:New_York_Mets) (1987), [Pittsburgh Pirates](:Pittsburgh_Pirates) (1987–88), and [Detroit Tigers](:Detroit_Tigers) (1989). Pedrique served as the [Houston Astros](:Houston_Astros) [bench coach](:Bench_coach) and as manager of the [Arizona Diamondbacks](:Arizona_Diamondbacks). He also served [first base coach](:First_base_coach) of the [Oakland Athletics](:Oakland_Athletics) a season before being shuffled to third base coaching for two further seasons. He is currently the third base coach for the [Miami Marlins](:Miami_Marlins)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
