<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Club_Nacional_de_Football> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Club Nacional de Football (Spanish pronunciation: [ˈkluβ nasjoˈnal de ˈfuðβol], National Football Club or simply as Nacional) is a Uruguayan professional sports club based in Montevideo. The club was founded on 14 May 1899 as a result of the merger between Uruguay Athletic Club and Montevideo Fútbol Club. Although its main focus is football, the club hosts many other activities, including basketball, futsal, tennis, cycling, volleyball, and chess. In February 2013, Nacional reached 60,000 associates."@en .
