<http://dbpedia.org/resource/First_baseman> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A first baseman, abbreviated 1B, is the player on a baseball or softball team who fields the area nearest first base, the first of four bases a baserunner must touch in succession to score a run. The first baseman is responsible for the majority of plays made at that base. In the numbering system used to record defensive plays, the first baseman is assigned the number 3."@en .
