<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Minnesota_Twins> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Minnesota Twins** are an American professional [baseball](:Baseball) team based in [Minneapolis](:Minneapolis). The Twins compete in [Major League Baseball](:Major_League_Baseball) (MLB) as a member club of the [American League](:American_League) (AL) [Central Division](:American_League_Central). The team is named after the [Twin Cities](:Minneapolis%E2%80%93Saint_Paul) area which includes the two adjoining cities of Minneapolis and [St. Paul](:Saint_Paul%2C_Minnesota).The franchise was founded in [Washington, D.C.](:Washington%2C_D%2EC%2E), in [1901](:1901_in_baseball) as the [Washington Senators](:Washington_Senators_%281901%E2%80%931960%29). The team [moved](:Major_League_Baseball_relocation_of_1950s%E2%80%9360s) to Minnesota and was renamed the Minnesota Twins for the start of the [1961 season](:1961_Major_League_Baseball_season). The Twins played in [Metropolitan Stadium](:Metropolitan_Stadium) from 1961 to 1981 and in the [Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome](:Hubert_H%2E_Humphrey_Metrodome) from 1982 to 2009. The team played its inaugural game at [Target Field](:Target_Field) on April 12, 2010. The franchise won the [World Series](:World_Series) in 1924 as the Senators, and in 1987 and 1991 as the Twins.From 1901 to 2021, the Senators/Twins franchise's overall regular-season win–loss–tie record is 9,012–9,716–109 (.481); as the Twins (through 2021), it is 4,789–4,852–8 (.497)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
