<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dublin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dublin** (; [Irish](:Irish_language): *Baile Átha Cliath*, Template:IPA-ga or Template:IPA-ga) is the capital and largest city of [Ireland](:Republic_of_Ireland). On a bay at the mouth of the [River Liffey](:River_Liffey), it is in the [province](:Provinces_of_Ireland) of [Leinster](:Leinster), bordered on the south by the Dublin Mountains, a part of the [Wicklow Mountains](:Wicklow_Mountains) range. At the [2016 census](:2016_census_of_Ireland), it had a population of 1,173,179, while the population of [County Dublin](:County_Dublin) as a whole was 1,347,359, and the [Greater Dublin Area](:Greater_Dublin_Area) was 1,904,806.A settlement was established in the area by the [Gaels](:Gaels) during or before the 7th century, followed by the [Vikings](:Viking). As the [Kingdom of Dublin](:Kings_of_Dublin) grew, it became Ireland's principal settlement by the 12th century [Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland](:Anglo-Norman_invasion_of_Ireland). The city expanded rapidly from the 17th century and was briefly the second largest in the [British Empire](:British_Empire) and sixth largest in [Western Europe](:Western_Europe) after the [Acts of Union](:Acts_of_Union_1800) in 1800. Following independence in 1922, Dublin became the capital of the [Irish Free State](:Irish_Free_State), [renamed Ireland](:Names_of_the_Irish_State) in 1937.Dublin is a centre for education, arts and culture, administration and industry. As of 2018[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Dublin&action=edit), the city was listed by the [Globalization and World Cities Research Network](:Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network) (GaWC) as a [global city](:Global_city), with a ranking of \"Alpha minus\", which places it as one of the top thirty cities in the world."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
