<http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_York_Mets> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **New York Mets** are an American [professional baseball](:Professional_baseball) team based in the [New York City borough](:Boroughs_of_New_York_City) of [Queens](:Queens). The Mets compete in [Major League Baseball](:Major_League_Baseball) (MLB) as a member of the [National League](:National_League) (NL) [East division](:National_League_East). They are one of two major league clubs based in New York City, the other being the [American League](:American_League)'s (AL) [New York Yankees](:New_York_Yankees). One of baseball's first [expansion teams](:Expansion_team), the Mets were founded in 1962 to replace New York's departed NL teams, the [Brooklyn Dodgers](:History_of_the_Brooklyn_Dodgers) and the [New York Giants](:History_of_the_New_York_Giants_%28baseball%29). The team's colors evoke the [blue](:Dodger_blue) of the Dodgers and the orange of the Giants.For the 1962 and 1963 seasons, the Mets played home games at the [Polo Grounds](:Polo_Grounds) in Manhattan before moving to Queens. From 1964 to 2008, the Mets played their home games at [Shea Stadium](:Shea_Stadium), named after [William Shea](:William_Shea), the founder of the [Continental League](:Continental_League), a proposed third major league, the announcement of which prompted their admission as an NL expansion team. Since 2009, the Mets have played their home games at [Citi Field](:Citi_Field) next to the site where Shea Stadium once stood.In their [inaugural season](:1962_New_York_Mets_season), the Mets posted a record of 40–120, the worst regular-season record since MLB went to a 162-game schedule. The team never finished better than second-to-last in the 1960s until the [\"Miracle Mets\"](:1969_New_York_Mets_season) beat the [Baltimore Orioles](:Baltimore_Orioles) in the [1969 World Series](:1969_World_Series), considered one of the biggest upsets in World Series history despite the Mets having [won 100 games](:List_of_Major_League_Baseball_100_win_seasons) that season. The Mets have qualified for the postseason ten times, winning the [World Series](:World_Series) twice (1969 and [1986](:1986_New_York_Mets_season%29) and winning five [National League pennants](:National_League) (most recently in [2000](:2000_New_York_Mets_season) and [2015](:2015_New_York_Mets_season%29), and six [National League East](:National_League_East) division titles.Since 2020, the Mets have been owned by billionaire hedge fund manager [Steve Cohen](:Steve_Cohen_%28businessman%29), who purchased the team for $2.4 billion. As of 2022, *[Forbes](:Forbes)* ranked the Mets as the sixth valuable [MLB team](:Major_League_Baseball), valued at $2.650 billion.As of the end of the 2022 regular season, the team's overall win–loss record is 4,652–4,988 (.483)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
