<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Covina,_California> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Covina** is a city in [Los Angeles County](:Los_Angeles_County%2C_California), [California](:California), United States, about 22 miles (35 km) east of downtown [Los Angeles](:Los_Angeles), in the [San Gabriel Valley](:San_Gabriel_Valley). The population was 51,268 according to the 2020 census, up from 47,796 at the 2010 census. The city's slogan, \"One Mile Square and All There\", was coined when the incorporated area of the city was only one square mile (2.6 km2).Covina is bordered by [West Covina](:West_Covina%2C_California), to its south and west side. [Irwindale](:Irwindale%2C_California) lies to the west, as well as the unincorporated area of [Vincent](:Vincent%2C_California), and the city of [Baldwin Park](:Baldwin_Park%2C_California). [Azusa](:Azusa%2C_California) and [Glendora](:Glendora%2C_California) are to the north, the unincorporated community of [Charter Oak](:Charter_Oak%2C_California) to the northeast, [San Dimas](:San_Dimas%2C_California) to the east, the unincorporated area of [Ramona](:Ramona%2C_California_%28Los_Angeles_County%29) and city of [Pomona](:Pomona%2C_California) to the southeast."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
