<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tom_Browning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Thomas Leo Browning** (born April 28, 1960) is a former [Major League Baseball](:Major_League_Baseball) [left-handed](:Left-handed) [pitcher](:Pitcher). During a 12-year baseball career, he pitched for the [Cincinnati Reds](:Cincinnati_Reds) (1984–1994) and the [Kansas City Royals](:Kansas_City_Royals) (1995). He is also co-author of *Tom Browning's Tales from the Reds Dugout*.Browning pitched the twelfth [perfect game](:Perfect_game_%28baseball%29) in baseball history on September 16, 1988, against the [Los Angeles Dodgers](:Los_Angeles_Dodgers). He also won the World Series with the Reds in 1990."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
